## 15. Certification Rule

Do not mark an API as:

```text
CERTIFIED
```

unless concrete runtime evidence exists.

Do not mark an API as:

```text
VERIFIED
```

based only on an architectural document.

Use:

```text
IDENTIFIED
```

when the API exists in the architecture.

Use:

```text
OBSERVED
```

when direct runtime behaviour has been captured.

Use:

```text
VERIFIED
```

when runtime behaviour has been compared against the approved contract.

Use:

```text
CERTIFIED
```

only after the required evidence chain has been completed.

